---
import BaseLayout from'../../../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Breadcrumbs from'../../../../components/Breadcrumbs.astro';
import LearningSection from'../../../../components/LearningSection.astro';
import Grade7CoordinateGrid from'../../../../components/Grade7CoordinateGrid.astro';
import Grade7Unit1ReviewPractice from'../../../../components/Grade7Unit1ReviewPractice.astro';
import{unit1CompletionCoverage}from'../../../../data/grade7Unit1Completion';
const base=import.meta.env.BASE_URL;
const lessonSlugs=['the-cartesian-plane','create-designs','transformations','horizontal-vertical-distances'];
---
<BaseLayout title="Unit 1 Review | Grade 7 Math" description="Review Coordinates and Design across Lessons 1.1–1.4 before the independent Unit Check." themeColor="#2457c5">
<div class="completion-page"><Breadcrumbs items={[{label:'Home',href:base},{label:'Grade 7 Math',href:`${base}courses/grade-7-math/`},{label:'Coordinates and Design'},{label:'Unit Review'}]}/>
<header class="hero"><p class="eyebrow">GRADE 7 MATH · UNIT 1 COMPLETION</p><h1>Coordinates and Design <span>Unit Review</span></h1><p>Retrieve the four lesson models, repair mixed questions with support, and finish with a four-part readiness check. This page reviews the verified Unit 1 mathematics without adding new coordinate methods.</p><div class="sequence" aria-label="Unit completion sequence"><a href="../horizontal-vertical-distances/">1.4 Lesson</a><strong aria-current="step">Unit Review</strong><a href="../unit-check/">Unit Check</a><a href="../math-arcade/">Math Arcade</a></div></header>

<LearningSection id="retrieve" eyebrow="RETRIEVE" title="Four lesson stations" icon="🧭" tone="idea"><p>Say the key idea before opening the lesson link. Each station points back to the exact verified model if you need a repair.</p><div class="stations">{unit1CompletionCoverage.map((item,i)=><article><p class="station-number">LESSON {item.lesson}</p><h2>{item.title}</h2><ul>{item.concepts.map(c=><li>{c}</li>)}</ul><a href={`../${lessonSlugs[i]}/#understand`}>Open verified Lesson {item.lesson} Understand →</a></article>)}</div></LearningSection>

<LearningSection id="examples" eyebrow="CONNECT THE IDEAS" title="Four representative worked examples" icon="🧩" tone="learn"><div class="examples">
 <article><h3>1 · Locate before you reason</h3><Grade7CoordinateGrid mode="static" points={[{x:-6,y:4,label:'P'},{x:0,y:-5,label:'Q'},{x:5,y:-3,label:'R'}]} title="Three review points on the Cartesian plane"/><p><strong>P(−6, 4)</strong> is in Quadrant II, <strong>Q(0, −5)</strong> is on the y-axis, and <strong>R(5, −3)</strong> is in Quadrant IV. Read x first, then y.</p></article>
 <article><h3>2 · Coordinates + connection order make the design</h3><Grade7CoordinateGrid mode="static" points={[{x:-5,y:3,label:'A'},{x:2,y:3,label:'B'},{x:2,y:-2,label:'C'},{x:-5,y:-2,label:'D'}]} title="Rectangle built from four labelled vertices"/><p>The vertex list locates the corners; <strong>A→B→C→D→A</strong> tells how to connect them. Changing only the order can change the picture even when all four coordinates are correct.</p></article>
 <article><h3>3 · Track image vertices</h3><Grade7CoordinateGrid mode="static" points={[{x:4,y:-3,label:'A'},{x:4,y:3,label:'A′'},{x:-2,y:4,label:'A″'}]} title="Successive images A, A prime, and A double prime"/><p>Reflecting A(4, −3) in the x-axis gives A′(4, 3). Translating A′ 6 left and 1 up gives A″(−2, 4). Keep corresponding labels matched through each step.</p></article>
 <article><h3>4 · Movement is not distance travelled</h3><Grade7CoordinateGrid mode="static" points={[{x:-5,y:4,label:'A'},{x:4,y:-3,label:'F'}]} title="Start and finish for a route comparison"/><p>From A to F, the net positional change is <strong>9 right and 7 down</strong>. A direct grid route travels 9 horizontal and 7 vertical units. A route that backtracks can reach the same finish while travelling farther.</p></article>
 </div></LearningSection>

<LearningSection id="practice" eyebrow="PRACTISE & REPAIR" title="Mixed supported review" icon="✏️" tone="practice"><Grade7Unit1ReviewPractice/></LearningSection>

<LearningSection id="scope" eyebrow="UNIT 1 BOUNDARY" title="What this review does—and does not assess" icon="🛡️" tone="review"><div class="scope-grid"><article><h3>Included</h3><p>Cartesian-plane location, ordered pairs, design vertices and connection order, translations/reflections/rotations, image notation, successive transformations, horizontal/vertical movement and distance, corresponding vertices, and route comparison.</p></article><article><h3>Not introduced here</h3><p>Diagonal distance formulas, Pythagorean distance, slope, vectors, mapping-rule algebra, or other higher-grade coordinate methods.</p></article></div></LearningSection>

<LearningSection id="next" eyebrow="NEXT" title="Move to the independent Unit Check" icon="🏁" tone="review"><p>Use the Unit Check only after the review feels secure. It uses a separate question bank, hides all correctness until the full attempt is submitted, and gives lesson-specific repair routes afterward.</p><div class="next-actions"><a class="primary" href="../unit-check/">Open independent Unit Check →</a><a href="../horizontal-vertical-distances/">← Return to Lesson 1.4</a></div></LearningSection>
</div></BaseLayout>
<style>
.completion-page{max-width:1180px;margin:auto;padding:1rem}.hero{padding:2rem 0 2.5rem}.hero .eyebrow,.station-number{font-size:.76rem;font-weight:900;letter-spacing:.08em;color:#607087}.hero h1{font-size:clamp(2.45rem,7vw,4.8rem);line-height:.98;margin:.35rem 0}.hero h1 span{display:block;color:#2457c5}.sequence{display:flex;gap:.45rem;flex-wrap:wrap;margin-top:1rem}.sequence a,.sequence strong{padding:.5rem .65rem;border-radius:999px;background:#eef3f9;color:#244260;text-decoration:none}.sequence strong{background:#2457c5;color:#fff}.stations,.examples,.scope-grid{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(2,minmax(0,1fr));gap:.8rem}.stations article,.examples article,.scope-grid article{min-width:0;padding:1rem;border:1px solid #d9e3ef;border-radius:14px;background:#fff}.stations h2,.examples h3{margin:.2rem 0}.stations a{font-weight:850;color:#174ea6}.next-actions{display:flex;gap:.7rem;flex-wrap:wrap;align-items:center}.next-actions a{padding:.7rem .85rem;border-radius:9px;font-weight:850;color:#174ea6}.next-actions .primary{background:#2457c5;color:#fff;text-decoration:none}.completion-page :focus-visible{outline:3px solid #ea8c00;outline-offset:3px}@media(max-width:760px){.stations,.examples,.scope-grid{grid-template-columns:1fr}}@media(max-width:390px){.completion-page{padding:.7rem}.hero h1{font-size:clamp(2.15rem,11vw,3rem)}.stations article,.examples article,.scope-grid article{padding:.75rem}}@media(prefers-reduced-motion:reduce){.completion-page *{animation:none!important;transition:none!important;scroll-behavior:auto!important}}
</style>
